					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2008-07-22 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3003/2694743696_dbfe50c670.jpg?v=0" onmouseover="undefined" onmouseout="undefined" alt="" title="undefined" width="375" height="500" /><div>HIP HOP PERIOD: RIVAL SHOWDOWN!</div><div><br /></div><div>FRIDAY, JULY 25</div><div>HIDMO ERITREAN CUISINE - 20th and JACKSON</div><div>DOORS 7:30PM</div><div>FREE FOR YOUTH</div><div>$5 ADULT ADMISSION</div><div><br /></div><div>FEATURING:</div><div>KHINGZ (ABYSSINIAN CREOLE)</div><div>1ST QUARTER STORM (ROGUE PINAY + EL DIA)</div><div>CANARY SING</div><div>LANGUAGE ARTS</div><div>KAMACHO</div><div>J-REYN</div><div>and DJ WD4D!</div><div><br /></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2008-07-18 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><br />TOMORROW - Saturday - the 19th - Alki beach...<br /><br />Common Market will be playing 4-5 songs LIVE on the air plus an interview -<br />all broadcasting live from the KNDD beachhouse on Alki! <br /><br />This show is ALL AGES and the weather is supposed to be great <br /><br />Saturday the 19th - they go live at 7PM sharp - come support!<br /><br />more info at http://1077theend.com/pages/2452445.php<br /><br />(Thanks to RAY for the great flyer!)<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2008-07-15 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><strong>Common Market</strong><br /><br />July 25<br /><br />4:30 pm :: All Ages<br /><br /><strong><br /><br />Mainstage, Capitol Hill Block Party</strong><br /><br /><br /><br />also...Girl Talk, Chromeo, The Physics, Vampire Weekend, Hold Steady and Devotchka<br /><br /><br /><br />more info at www.capitolhillblockparty.com<br /><br /><br /><br />_____________________________________<br /><br /><br /><br /><strong>Monday July 28th</strong><br /><br /><br /><br />The Paramount<br /><br /><br /><br /><strong>Matisyahu with special guests - Common Market</strong><br /><br /><img src="http://i29.photobucket.com/albums/c271/SCIONtificrecords/MATIS_SEATTLE_POSTERindd.jpg" alt="" width="414" height="640" /><br /><br />tickets at Ticketmaster.com<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2008-07-13 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>if you haven&#39;t already, head on over to www.bluescholars.com to peep the updates with Blue Scholars as we continue on the <strong>Freshly Dipped Tour</strong>.<br /><br />finally got a lens for the camera, then realized that the battery was dead and the charger was in Seattle. stay posted tho! flics coming within 30 hours!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2008-06-12 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><img src="http://i25.tinypic.com/10gxtea.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br /><strong>THIS FRIDAY NIGHT!<br />A FUNDRAISER FOR HIDMO ERITREAN CUISINE<br />FEATURING</strong><br /><br /><strong>BLUE SCHOLARS</strong><br />Grizz Gang<br />Boombox Party DJs<br /><br />Hosted by Abysinnian Creole<br />(Khingz and Gabriel Teodros)<br /><br />Friday, June 13<br />Youngstown Cultural Arts Center<br />(4408 Delridge Way South in West Seattle)<br />8:00pm - 11:00pm<br /><strong>TICKETS: <a href="www.hidmo.org">www.hidmo.org<br /></a></strong><br /><strong>HAPPY BIRTHDAY RAHWA! SUPPORT THE HIDMO!</strong><br /><br /><div align="left">Message from Rahwa, owner of Hidmo Eritrean Cuisine: <em>Hidmo has survived many challenges this year (go online for story
links) and we have handled these difficulties with varying degrees of
frustration, confusion and anger but always with hope in our hearts.
Because every time something threatens to knock us out, we stay
standing, held up by the many hands that reach out to give us support.
The hands of individuals in this community that see the value in our
existence. The things that have been accomplished within Hidmo this
year are truly phenomenal. We have housed a youth organization and two
regular community-led events that draw not only the best talent in the
city but also makes art available to individuals of all ages on a
regular basis. We have become a neighborhood touchstone, one of the few
left, where persons of any background can come as they are and just be.
We have changed the outlook of local youth, who used to see the place
where they lived as an unsafe battleground, but now see it as a home,
and themselves as active participants in a community. We have provided
the space for countless groups and individuals to meet, organize and
work... and we are just getting started!</em></div></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> [3] <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=23